Well, I finally ascended again, after losing a knight on astral, and a
promising healer and samuri.  This was my first ascention where I recieved
no wishes until the castle, and found no bones files (well, no helpful ones.
I did run into a samuri that somehow left a skeleton wandering around on
dlvl 6, but had no weapons or items I wanted).  So this one feels good.  One
of the more interesting things happened when I first visited minetown, which
was coaligned.  I figured I'd camp here for a long while.  Well, a nymph
quaffed a potion of invisibility, and without see invisible (and my speed
stolen by that skeleton I mentioned earlier), it basically boiled down to me
losing a random item every 50 turns or so.  So I headed further down,
without anyhting better than Excalibur.  Hit a polytrap, which morphed me
into a gray dragon.  An earlier polytrap had made Sam(uel) into Sam(antha),
so I laid a couple eggs.  One survived long enough to wipe out some
shopkeeps, giving me a large amount for protection.  I hit sokobon, got the
amulet of reflection, but still had no MR.  So I hit minetown again for some
sacc festing, during which the foolish nymph stole a /oSleep.  The next time
I saw her my amulet reflected the attack, and she was asleep.  After that it
wasn't long till I had Frostbrand.  I really wanted to #twoweapon
Grayswandir and a silver saber, but hey, I'll take what I can get.


Later on, I was doing some sac/praying on dlvl 10 or so, getting a ton of hp
from golden glows.  Still didnt have MR, so I skipped the quest, and headed
to the castle.  On the way down, got some silver dragon scales, and made
some SDSM (better than plate mail...)  Also had some +5 GoP, so I had decent
AC, figured the castle (with conflict) would get me a wish, and I could get
a CoMR.  I couldn't levitate, so I skipped medusa, and jumped through a hole
to the castle,  right into the arms of an Arch-Lich, who blew off my boots
and eventually my armor.  He ran to medusa, so I followed.  A Master lich
followed as well.  With conflict on, Medusa killed the master, but not the
arch, so I hit the persus statue and got a shield of reflection.  Didn't
think much of it, cleared the castle, and got some gray scales.  So I
figured GDSM/Shield of Reflection would be a good combo, so I did that for a
bit, and then decided to hang out in the higher levels before doing
gehennom.  Wished for a HoT, charging scrolls, boots of speed, magic marker,
and a bag of holding (up till then, I had no bag at all).  That was all.  I
hadn't gotten an early wish, and the castle wand was (0:1).... darn RNG



Headed back to my lowest altar to sac a bit, and lo and behold, I got
Grayswandir! Well, I never found a silver saber, and at this point I was
pretty much stuck with GDSM and SoR, so I couldn't #twoweapon anyway.  Went
to gehennom, polypiled and eventually got =oFA and =oLev.  Found a magic
lamp, and got a MM from it, to fully enchant Grayswandir and build up my
armor.  Got another wish from Vlad's throne, another MM, made some gold
detection scrolls, some more enchant armors, and it turned out Grayswandir
ate around 5 enchant weapons to make +7.  Down and back again, no big
surprises, the mysterious force seemed abnormally annoying, I spent more
time I lvls 44 and 42 than I wanted to.  It even kicked in when I used
c!oGL, which I didn't know could happen.


Died once on Air, those Air Elementals never gave me so much trouble.  Twice
I was struck by lightning or some such, which froze me a couple turns.  If I
had thought ahead and brought a potion of full healing or two, I would have
survived, but I had some many "oLS, I really didn't mind burning one up.
